      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checking the code, I\u0027m not sure we have any non-memmap way of reading the lid angle (we don\u0027t seem to store it for non-UPDATE_HOST_MEM_MAP config).\n\nI think this code would be acceptable if we can skip this check entirely for ECs that don\u0027t define UPDATE_HOST_MEM_MAP (otherwise that\u0027s the result? error, or unpredictable data returned?). Is there some way ectool can determine if memory map is configured on the EC side?\n\nIf not, I think we should just move this to an entirely new ectool command.",
      "parentUuid": "5b2a4b7b_19e07e17",
      "revId": "4754ff4410d00a97c25e7f3bfea372bfebf0d961",
