      "writtenOn": "2015-11-19T22:35:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on checking the code, if system does not support memmap, then the host command should fail and exit ectool. For this specific motionsense command, the user should see the XYZ value for the sensors, then ectool error and exit.\n\nI did thinking about adding a new host command or a motionsense new sub-command to return the value from motion_lid_get_angle(), it should work for non-memmap system, but then it will take extra code space which could still be a concern for kunimitsu. It will not be a huge amount of new code, but just a precaution until all other required features are implemented.\n\nDo you have any plan/idea on how to fix other commands that use memmap? I was thinking about adding an ALS read to ectool via memmap as well, but I will not do it now unless I have a better direction on this.",
